ds-2-iranians-over-alleged-antisemitic-terror-plot/a-79532184?maca=en-rss-en-world-4025-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The pair were arrested on the eve of Yom Kippur and later charged with plotting to attack Jewish targets in Manchester.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Flydubai co-pilot attempted 'terrorist attack,' UAE says</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:c3d01fb3ebe59a13ecff8a7196325d1181ed39867b9b5b298fab41ea22214464</id><updated>2026-10-05T05:55:14Z</updated><published>2026-10-03T08:17:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/flydubai-co-pilot-attempted-terrorist-attack-uae-says/a-79526641--5d350a043c31.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/flydubai-co-pilot-attempted-terrorist-attack-uae-says/a-79526641?maca=en-rss-en-world-4025-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The man, who stabbed his fellow pilot on an Israel-bound Flydubai flight, was reportedly barred from flying in his native Oman over security concerns.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Morocco's first female head of government: Symbol or real reform?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:fd997edeafcc0df1238cde93f76b881cf5f62b6ebe603372daa9fc66590fe3a0</id><updated>2026-10-05T05:55:14Z</updated><published>2026-10-03T08:10:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/morocco-s-first-female-head-of-government-symbol-or-real-reform/a-79521808--5c6131d5d637.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/morocco-s-first-female-head-of-government-symbol-or-real-reform/a-79521808?maca=en-rss-en-world-4025-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Fatima Zahra Mansouri has been chosen as Morocco's first female prime minister. Is her appointment a kind of symbolism, to show Morocco in a positive light? Or could Mansouri bring genuine changes for Moroccan women?</summary><category term="Africa" /></entry><entry><title>Bosnia and Herzegovina is still shaped by war, separatism, EU ambitions</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:b216d06a34982b089c1ff5171f95622a3550d0869db327060967830eebe9319b</id><updated>2026-10-05T05:55:14Z</updated><published>2026-10-03T06:51:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/bosnia-and-herzegovina-is-still-shaped-by-war-separatism-eu-ambitions/a-79523557--c6b59bb6d492.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/bosnia-and-herzegovina-is-still-shaped-by-war-separatism-eu-ambitions/a-79523557?maca=en-rss-en-world-4025-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Bosnia and Herzegovina is governed by a system established after the Bosnian war — more than 30 years ago. Ethnic divisions, a complex administration and European integration all shape the country's political reality.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Australia: Car crashes into rugby fans, 10 injured</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:d1b982b67e8493942f816f6a1168411b29e792fd9590c13bd29ebd6a302dba33</id><updated>2026-10-05T05:55:14Z</updated><published>2026-10-03T04:27:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/australia-car-crashes-into-rugby-fans-10-injured/a-79526643--1bdc3d304c0b.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/australia-car-crashes-into-rugby-fans-10-injured/a-79526643?maca=en-rss-en-world-4025-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The driver has been identified as an 18-year-old man who is said to have been "revving" when he lost control of his car.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Spain's parliament rejects housing bill as protests continue</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:13f5fcf8e99599c721f5e2c52c0f23df386136e59ee180a22d9d4e13b292438c</id><updated>2026-10-05T05:55:14Z</updated><published>2026-10-02T16:39:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/spain-s-parliament-rejects-housing-bill-as-protests-continue/a-79522683--f3b2b2f36991.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/s